=== SURVEY ===
Web source BreadcrumbOverridesContext.tsx is a transparent React-context coordination primitive — it
renders NO chrome of its own. A `BreadcrumbOverridesProvider` holds a `Map<number, BreadcrumbOverrideMap>`
of per-page registrations; pages call `useSetBreadcrumbOverrides({...})` inside an effect to push their
dynamic route-label overrides (e.g. `{ '/drives/:id': '196th St → NE 90th' }`), JSON-comparing the map
so an identical literal does not re-register; the provider memo merges every registration (later wins per
route key, empty labels dropped) and exposes `{ overrides, register, unregister }`. `useBreadcrumbOverrides()`
reads the merged map (or `{}` outside a provider). Layout forwards it into `useBreadcrumbs(overrides)`
(hooks/useBreadcrumbs.ts), which matches the current path against ROUTE_META (first match), walks the
parent chain (cycle-broken), resolves each label (override > i18n key > default), substitutes `{{param}}`
in labels and `:param` in hrefs, and returns the trail leaf-last; `<Breadcrumbs>` (components/layout/
Breadcrumbs.tsx) renders it (Home icon, chevron separators, truncation, trailing item link-less) and
self-suppresses for <= 1 item.
Data sources (P1/S8): useBreadcrumbOverrides, useSetBreadcrumbOverrides, useBreadcrumbs. Shared
components: none. Charts/maps: none. i18n keys extracted from source: none (anonymous surface; the
renderer it feeds uses a11y.breadcrumb / a11y.breadcrumbHome).
Existing native: no Breadcrumb* symbols collide (only LegacyAlert*Redirect*Breadcrumb* prefixed types
exist) → no duplicate-symbol risk. Canonical surface pattern studied + mirrored: the closest committed
analogue shared-surfaces/ChartHiddenSeriesContext.* (a React-context state-holder: Adapter / Projection /
Model / .swift / Views / Previews / strings / Tests / AdapterTests).

=== REASONING ===
- The web source is a coordination primitive (no fetch, no remote data); SwiftUI's idiomatic React-context
  equivalent is an Environment value. Chosen architecture mirrors ChartHiddenSeriesContext exactly:
  • Adapter (pure, Foundation): surface slug; BreadcrumbOverrideMap; BreadcrumbOverridesReducer (sanitize
    drop-empty + ascending-id later-wins merge + JSON-stable signature = web serialised); RouteMeta +
    ordered RouteTable (= ROUTE_META, ordered for deterministic first-match + indexed for parent walk);
    PathMatch (= matchPath end:true, :param capture); TrailItem; TrailBuilder (verbatim useBreadcrumbs:
    match → walk parents cycle-broken → label override>i18n>default → {{param}}/:param fill → leaf-last).
    The i18n lookup is an injected @Sendable closure so the core is Foundation-only + deterministic.
  • Projection (pure): TrailResolved (items / isEmpty / isSuppressed=`<=1` / isRendered / current /
    ancestors / count / appliedOverrideCount) + projection (cached overrides + route → resolved trail).
  • Model: BreadcrumbOverridesStore (@MainActor @Observable registrations map = web provider state:
    register skips unchanged content, unregister no-ops unknown id, monotonic ids, later-wins merged,
    reset, shared singleton); BreadcrumbOverridesState (the context value { overrides, register,
    unregister } + view.opened-once + stop-does-not-clear); Strings i18n facade; Telemetry seam + OSLog.
  • .swift: EnvironmentValues.breadcrumbOverridesState (the React context); BreadcrumbOverridesProvider
    (owns the state, injects env, view.opened on appear); BreadcrumbOverridesReader (= useBreadcrumbOverrides
    render-prop, hands the merged map / {} outside a provider); .breadcrumbOverridesProvider() +
    .setBreadcrumbOverrides(_:) modifiers (the latter = useSetBreadcrumbOverrides: register on appear +
    on signature change, unregister on disappear/empty, JSON-stable, inert outside a provider).
  • Views: BreadcrumbOverridesTrailView (= Breadcrumbs.tsx: Home SF Symbol, chevron.right separators,
    200pt truncation, trailing item bold link-less, self-suppress <= 1) + DEBUG inspector staging EVERY
    real branch; Previews per branch; strings table; Tests + AdapterTests.
- States rendered: the source has NO loading/error/stale/offline (no fetch) — inventing that chrome would
  contradict the spec (covenant 5). The REAL branches are reproduced + each rendered visibly in the DEBUG
  inspector (never a blank box): override-applied trail, route-default trail, suppressed top-level (single
  item → friendly "breadcrumb hidden" note), unknown route (empty → friendly "route not registered" note),
  and the no-provider/inert branch. The production trail view self-suppresses exactly like the web renderer.
- Native adaptation (documented, not a shortcut): web hides middle crumbs behind an ellipsis on narrow
  screens; the idiomatic Apple treatment is a horizontal scroll keeping every crumb reachable — data,
  order, links, truncation + suppression are reproduced identically.
- Rejected: porting Tailwind/sr-only literally; a truly invisible surface (the inspector renders branches
  visibly); HTTP in the view (none — pure in-process store, like the web React state).

